{#
---
name: irb-n-ip
summary: Additional IPv4 prefixes on an IRB, driven by VN tags
config_style: junos
section: top_level_set_delete
roles: [leaf]
category: misc
status: active
requires:
  vars: [vxlan, vlan, role]
  tags: ['irb-ip/<address>/<len>']
author: kimcharli@gmail.com
tested_on: ["6.1.2-28"]
updated: 2026-08-11
changelog:
  - 2026-08-11 implement tag-driven multi-prefix IRB
---
Apstra models one gateway prefix per Virtual Network. This configlet adds
further IPv4 prefixes to an IRB for the VLANs that need more than one.

Attach one tag per extra prefix to the VN, prefix length included:

  irb-ip/10.0.200.9/24
  irb-ip/192.168.20.1/24

No ordinal in the tag - Junos does not order addresses, and one tag per
address means adding or removing one never renumbers the others. Tags are
rendered sorted so the pushed diff is stable across regenerations.

The Apstra anycast gateway is re-stated first as `primary`. Junos otherwise
elects the numerically lowest address on the interface as primary, so adding a
lower extra prefix would silently move the source address of locally-generated
traffic off the gateway.

No routing-instance loop: the address is set under [edit interfaces], and
Apstra has already bound irb.<vlan_id> into its Routing Zone.

Leaf-only, tested on the first guard line so spines and access switches skip
the VN loop entirely. IRB_IP_TAG is deliberately set *above* that guard: a
{% set %} inside an {% if %} is reported as a missing configlet variable by the
Apstra validator, so moving it inside would fail the load. The `roles:` key
above is metadata and does not gate anything.

A tag carries one anycast address, so the identical value lands on every leaf
the VN is bound to. There is no per-leaf address and no virtual-gateway-address
on the extra prefixes - they are gateway-only. A tag cannot express a per-leaf
unique address, so a prefix that needs one (an OSPF or BGP adjacency sourced
from that subnet) is out of scope for this configlet.
-#}
{% set IRB_IP_TAG = 'irb-ip/' %}
{% if role == 'leaf' %}{# LEAF_ONLY #}
{% for vn in vxlan.values() | sort(attribute='vlan_id') %}{# VXLAN_DICT #}
{% set ns = namespace(ips=[]) %}
{% for tag in vn.tags | default([], True) | sort %}
{% if tag.startswith(IRB_IP_TAG) %}{% set ns.ips = ns.ips + [tag.split('/', 1)[1]] %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{# vlan_value is a read-only alias for the native entry; vxlan/vlan are not modified #}
{% set vlan_value = vlan[vn.vlan_id | string] %}
{% if ns.ips %}{# TAGGED_VN #}
set interfaces irb unit {{ vn.vlan_id }} family inet address {{ vlan_value.fhrp_ipv4_address }}/{{ vlan_value.ipv4_prefixlen }} primary
{% for ip in ns.ips %}
set interfaces irb unit {{ vn.vlan_id }} family inet address {{ ip }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}{# TAGGED_VN #}
{% endfor %}{# VXLAN_DICT #}
{% endif %}{# LEAF_ONLY #}
